-- ==========================================
-- MOVEMENT SCRIPT v16
-- ==========================================
-- FIXES vs v15:
--
-- FIX 1 – Jump target landing ON the laser
--   v15 used:  laser.CFrame * Vector3.new(X, 0, -side*15)
--   CFrame * Vector3 TRANSFORMS the point into world space relative
--   to the laser pivot, so the target was sitting right on the beam.
--   Fixed: compute the far-side world position by taking the player's
--   XZ position, then stepping PAST the laser along the laser's local
--   Z axis in world space. Pure flat arithmetic, no CFrame multiply.
--
-- FIX 2 – Visualiser only visible when laser already close
--   collectThreats() cut off lasers at AGGRO_DISTANCE before they
--   entered the threats table, so the arc only drew when the laser
--   was already nearly on top of the player.
--   Fixed: separate "visual range" (VIZ_RANGE = 40 studs) tracked
--   outside collectThreats. Arc is drawn whenever any laser is within
--   VIZ_RANGE, even if it is not yet an active threat.
--
-- FIX 3 – Planner choosing bad waypoints → erratic movement
--   predictArc used:  laser.CFrame - laser.Position + (laser.Position + vel*t)
--   This translated the CFrame's position but left its ROTATION unchanged,
--   so for rotating lasers the hitbox was in completely the wrong place.
--   Fixed: store the laser's angular velocity (rad/s around Y) and build
--   the future CFrame as CFrame.new(futurePos) * CFrame.Angles(0, angle*t, 0)
--   so both position AND rotation are projected forward correctly.
-- ==========================================
